{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/pulls/9","id":4153671657,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTVpH8873k__p","html_url":"https://github.com/flowercomputers/bogkit/pull/9","diff_url":"https://github.com/flowercomputers/bogkit/pull/9.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/flowercomputers/bogkit/pull/9.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/issues/9","number":9,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[LAB] Daily simulated-developer feedback for BogKit","user":{"login":"urcades","id":1195363,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTUzNjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1195363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/urcades","html_url":"https://github.com/urcades","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urcades/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urcades/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urcades/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urcades/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urcades/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urcades/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urcades/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urcades/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/urcades/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Note: directly inspired by: https://gist.github.com/VictorTaelin/d632f46aa55e561d3cd2c43c66f2813e\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nThis long-lived draft PR is the evidence archive and discussion thread for a daily simulated-developer feedback lab.\r\n\r\nEvery run gives two fresh developer personas realistic existing-software problems before they inspect BogKit. They begin with the public onboarding surface, build the smallest meaningful integration or no-fit reproducer, run it, and record the complete friction trail. A separate skeptical reviewer reproduces material claims and rejects unsupported or bloated recommendations.\r\n\r\n## Boundaries\r\n\r\n- Daily changes stay under `developer-simulation/`.\r\n- The automation never changes BogKit core or existing examples automatically.\r\n- A trial may conclude that BogKit is not a fit.\r\n- Generated data, credentials, databases, build output, and unjustified large dependencies are never archived.\r\n- Findings remain proposals until a maintainer explicitly approves separate implementation work.\r\n- This PR is intentionally long-lived and should remain draft rather than being merged.\r\n\r\n## Reporting\r\n\r\n- Each day gets one immutable PR comment containing the verified report.\r\n- One rolling dashboard comment tracks coverage, recurring evidence, confirmed defects, no-fit signals, and candidate improvements.\r\n- A suggestion becomes a candidate only after two independent trials or one serious reproducible correctness defect.\r\n\r\n## Inaugural run\r\n\r\nThe first two trials cover:\r\n\r\n1. A PostgreSQL purchase-approval audit timeline requiring one transaction and role-protected immutability.\r\n2. Offline warehouse scanner reconciliation under duplicate, reordered, interrupted, and conflicting uploads.\r\n\r\nBoth produced runnable archives. Neither justified adding BogKit to the specified production architecture. The repeated, evidence-backed improvement is a concise onboarding capability matrix describing embedded storage, transaction, single-writer, and component boundaries.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- 15 inaugural trial tests passed.\r\n- Strict lint passed with warnings denied.\r\n- All archived Rust sources passed formatting checks.\r\n- Both demonstrations ran successfully.\r\n- The 20,000-operation synthetic threshold passed.\r\n- All 45 existing BogKit unit and documentation tests passed.\r\n- A skeptical review reproduced the major claims and removed overclaims and speculative API proposals.\r\n\r\nSee `developer-simulation/README.md` for the protocol and `developer-simulation/reports/2026-07-28.md` for the first full report.","created_at":"2026-07-28T17:20:23Z","updated_at":"2026-08-16T13:51:57Z","closed_at":"2026-08-16T13:51:57Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"8f01bdaed8d5184f18456fc9deb1785de4d7ba15","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/pulls/9/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/pulls/9/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/issues/9/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/statuses/0e9086e3ab0db0d35f9074dc27d4e94d609dcc5b","head":{"label":"flowercomputers:ed/developer-simulation","ref":"ed/developer-simulation","sha":"0e9086e3ab0db0d35f9074dc27d4e94d609dcc5b","user":{"login":"flowercomputers","id":169509703,"node_id":"O_kgDOChqDRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169509703?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/flowercomputers","html_url":"https://github.com/flowercomputers","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flowercomputers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flowercomputers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flowercomputers/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flowercomputers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flowercomputers/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flowercomputers/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flowercomputers/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flowercomputers/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flowercomputers/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":f